import Lampe
import Lampe.Crypto.Aes128

/-!
# AES-128-CBC reference test vectors

Validates `Lampe.Crypto.Aes128.aes128CbcEncryptPkcs7` (PKCS#7-padded
AES-128-CBC) against five independent vectors via `native_decide`.

The third vector is **NIST SP 800-38A Appendix F.2.1** ("CBC-AES128.Encrypt"):
- key = 2b7e151628aed2a6abf7158809cf4f3c
- IV  = 000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f
- 4-block plaintext from §F.2.1
- Expected ciphertext from §F.2.1 (the first 64 bytes), followed by
  the encryption of a full PKCS#7 padding block (0x10 × 16) — which is
  what our wrapper produces and what every conformant AES-128-CBC +
  PKCS#7 implementation produces (verified against the `cryptography`
  library in `scripts/gen/aes128_ref.py`).

Reference: NIST SP 800-38A,
https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/Legacy/SP/nistspecialpublication800-38a.pdf
-/

namespace Tests.Aes128

open Lampe.Crypto.Aes128

